# Keeps the build context small and secrets out (CONVENTIONS.md § 2). The Dockerfile
# itself arrives with DD.1; this file exists from the scaffold so the module never has a
# window in which a stray .env or node_modules could be sent to a daemon.
.git
node_modules
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
build
.docusaurus
screenshots/test-results
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.env*
